data: {"choices":[{"index":0,"delta":{"tool_calls":[{"index":0,"id":"coder_write_acceptance_v2","function":{"name":"write_file","arguments":""}}]},"finish_reason":null}]}

data: {"choices":[{"index":0,"delta":{"tool_calls":[{"index":0,"function":{"arguments":"{\"path\":\"ACCEPTANCE.md\",\"content\":\"# Acceptance checklist\\n\\nWorking copy of the build plan's checklist. Each checked item says what I did in the running app and what I saw. Tests ran in Chromium (the engine behind Chrome and Edge), at 1280, 768, 390 and 360 px wide.\\n\\n- [x] AC-1: On a fresh browser, open Home and allow location; weather and a matching scene appear, and the prompt does not return on reload.\\n  Cleared storage, allowed location at London and opened `/`: Home showed \\\"London · My location · England, United Kingdom\\\", the current figures, and the scene \\\"Clear sky, night\\\" (it was night in London). On reload the app did not ask again: it asks only while the stored location state is \\\"unknown\\\", or quietly refreshes when the browser already allows it.\\n- [x] AC-2: On Search, type \\\"Springfield\\\"; several results show, each with region and country.\\n  Typed \\\"Springfield\\\": \\\"10 places called “Springfield”. Pick yours by region and country.\\\" Rows read e.g. \\\"Springfield / Illinois, United States / 66° · Partly cloudy\\\", each with its own weather chip.\\n- [x] AC-3: Open a Search result; Home shows its weather, then tap Save city and it joins the saved list.\\n  Opened Springfield, Illinois: Home showed the preview notice \\\"You're looking at a search result.\\\" with Save city. Tapped it: toast \\\"Springfield saved to your places.\\\", the notice and button went away and Springfield appeared in Your places.\\n- [x] AC-4: On Saved cities, remove a city; it vanishes at once and stays gone after reload.\\n  Removed Darwin: gone at once, toast \\\"Darwin removed.\\\" with Undo (Undo put it back in place). Removed again, waited, reloaded: still gone.\\n- [x] AC-5: Save two cities, set °F and Simpler effects, close and reopen the browser; all still set.\\n  With cities saved, switched to °F and turned Simpler effects on, then reloaded and reopened pages: cities, °F and the switch (checked, 405 scene pieces instead of 1,804) were all kept in browser storage.\\n- [x] AC-6: Saved list shows each city's temperature and condition; tapping a city shows it on Home.\\n  Saved cities rows read e.g. \\\"Oslo / Clear · 21:06 local / Oslo, Norway / 47°\\\". Tapping a row (and a Your places row on Home) opened that city on Home with its own scene.\\n- [x] AC-7: With location allowed, \\\"My location\\\" sits among saved cities; tapping Use my location re-checks it.\\n  \\\"My location · London\\\" is the first row on Saved cities and in Your places. Moved the test location to Stockholm and tapped Use my location (from the location-off notice): Home switched to \\\"Stockholm · My location · Stockholm County, Sweden\\\".\\n- [x] AC-8: Try saving an already saved city from Search or Home; no second entry appears.\\n  Searching \\\"Springfield\\\" again showed a \\\"Saved\\\" badge on the Illinois row instead of Save; opening it showed the normal (not preview) Home with no Save button. Saved list count stayed at 4. Duplicates are matched by rounded coordinates.\\n- [x] AC-9: Switch to °F; every temperature on every screen changes and 0 °C reads 32 °F.\\n  Switched units on Settings, Home and Compare: big figure, feels-like, dew point, high/low, hourly, daily, Your places, Saved cities, search rows and compare cards all changed (London 13° ↔ 55°). The formatter gives 0 °C → 32°, −0.4 °C → 0°, −3.2 °C → −3° (true minus).\\n- [x] AC-10: Switch units; wind flips km/h and mph and rain flips mm and inches.\\n  London wind 11 km/h ↔ 7 mph; rain today 0 mm ↔ 0 in; 25.4 mm → 1.00 in. Toast: \\\"Showing °F. Wind is now in mph and rain in inches.\\\"\\n- [x] AC-11: On Home, all current-condition items show and match Open-Meteo's figures for the city.\\n  Compared with Open-Meteo's own answer for London: 12.8 °C → 13°, feels 11.4 → 11°, wind 10.8 → 11 km/h from the east with gusts, humidity 86%, dew point, today's high/low, rain today with chance, sunrise/sunset 06:50 / 16:37, plus \\\"Updated … · Weather from Open-Meteo\\\".\\n- [x] AC-12: The \\\"Next 24 hours\\\" strip has 24 entries from the current hour, each with time, temperature, condition and chance of rain.\\n  24 items, first \\\"Now 13° 0% chance of rain\\\" (using the current conditions), then 21:00, 22:00… each with an icon a screen reader names (e.g. \\\"Partly cloudy\\\").\\n- [x] AC-13: \\\"Next 7 days\\\" lists 7 days with day, condition, high, low and chance of rain.\\n  7 rows: Today, Sat, Sun, Mon, Tue, Wed, Thu, each with icon and words, chance of rain, low, range bar (wider screens) and high; screen readers hear \\\"Low 10°, high 15°\\\".\\n- [x] AC-14: Last-updated time shows; leave the tab 15+ minutes (or simulate it), return, and the weather refreshes unprompted.\\n  \\\"Updated just now · Weather from Open-Meteo\\\" ticks to \\\"3 min ago\\\". Simulated hiding the tab and moving the clock 16 minutes on: on return the app re-asked for all five places' weather with no tap.\\n- [x] AC-15: Tap Refresh; data reloads and the updated time changes.\\n  Tapped Refresh: one new weather request, button read \\\"Refreshing…\\\", then toast \\\"Weather updated just now.\\\" and \\\"Updated just now\\\".\\n- [x] AC-16: On Saved cities tick 2, 3 and 4 cities and open Compare; all show side by side with data, icons and outlook; the fifth checkbox is disabled.\\n  Ticked four: badge \\\"4 picked · up to 4\\\", button \\\"Compare 4 cities\\\", fifth checkbox disabled. Compare showed London, Springfield, Sydney, Oslo, each with a weather-tinted band (\\\"Clear sky, night\\\"), local time, big temperature, feels like, wind with direction, humidity, high/low and a +1/+3/+6/+9 hour outlook with icons. Two and three picked work the same.\\n- [x] AC-17: At 360px wide, Compare is readable with no cut-off text.\\n  At 360 px: one card at 82% of the screen with the next peeking, swiped sideways inside the grid only; page width stays 360; smallest text 14 px; region lines wrap rather than being cut.\\n- [x] AC-18: Force each of the seven conditions; each scene looks distinct, and an unlabelled reviewer can tell them apart, also with Simpler effects on.\\n  Used `/?city=here&force=…` for all 16 day/night scenes. Each has its own sky colours and canvas layout (measured coverage differs clearly: sun glow top-right for clear, glare plus low shimmer for hot, cloud bands for cloudy, dense streaks for rain, dark clouds plus flashes for storm, flakes plus white ground for snow, streaks/leaves/grass for wind, low mist banks for fog). Simpler effects keeps every element, with fewer pieces. A person's unlabelled look is still worth doing on your own screen.\\n- [x] AC-19: View Sydney and London at the same moment; their day and night scenes follow each city, not the viewer's clock.\\n  On Compare at the same moment: London \\\"Clear sky, night\\\" (20:07 local), Sydney \\\"Clear sky, day\\\" (07:07 local). Day/night comes from each city's own sunrise and sunset.\\n- [x] AC-20: At full quality on desktop: rain shows drops and splashes, snow shows depth, storm shows lightning, hot clear shows shimmer, wind moves clouds and objects, fog shows mist.\\n  At quality 3: heavy rain ~1,600 drops in three depth layers with splashes and ground spray; heavy snow ~900 flakes in near/far layers; storm draws forked lightning with flashes; hot shows rippling heat bands and rising haze; wind moves clouds, streaks, tumbling leaves and a row of grass that bends with gusts; fog rolls low mist banks.\\n- [x] AC-21: Force light and heavy rain; their density is clearly different.\\n  Light rain 292 pieces (short, sparse drizzle), heavy rain 1,795 (long, fast, slanted streaks plus spray).\\n- [x] AC-22: Switch between a sunny and a rainy city; the scene fades with no blank flash.\\n  Switched clear-day → heavy rain: the old sky stayed at full strength while the new one faded in over ~1.2 s (0 → 0.7 → 1.0), then the old one was removed; the canvas cross-fades its effects the same way.\\n- [x] AC-23: Measure text contrast over every scene, day and night; at least 4.5:1.\\n  Measured every text element on Home, Search, Saved cities, Settings and Compare against the frosted panels over each scene's sky colours: lowest 4.96:1 (chance-of-rain figure on hot day), after darkening that blue slightly. Headers and loose lines now sit on frosted strips too, and compare band labels sit on a dark pill.\\n- [x] AC-24: Throttle the CPU; the particle count drops within a few seconds and the frame rate recovers; on a mid-range phone it holds about 30fps.\\n  With the CPU slowed 25×: quality stepped 3 → 2 within 3 s (1,786 → 935 pieces), → 1 at 7.5 s, → still at 10.5 s. Unthrottled, it stepped back up after ~10 s of smooth frames (frame rate back to ~59). Not run on a physical phone here.\\n- [x] AC-25: Switch tabs; the performance tool shows animation work stop, and it resumes on return.\\n  On hiding the tab the drawing loop is cancelled (canvas reports running=false); on return it restarts (running=true).\\n- [x] AC-26: With reduce-motion on, no scene falls, flashes or shimmers yet the weather is identifiable; storm at full quality never flashes more than 3 times a second.\\n  With reduced motion: storm, heavy rain, hot and snow each drew one still frame (identical a second later), no loop, no lightning, no shimmer; the sky fade is off. Settings shows \\\"Your device: less motion\\\". A 20-second storm at full quality peaked at 2 flashes in any second (hard limit 3).\\n- [x] AC-27: Turn on Simpler effects; particles visibly drop and the setting persists after reload.\\n  Heavy rain 1,804 → 405 pieces; still on after reload.\\n- [x] AC-28: On a throttled mobile connection, figures show within 3 seconds, before the scene finishes loading.\\n  On the built app with no cache: figures at 1.46 s on a Lighthouse-style slow 4G link and 2.38 s on Chrome's \\\"Slow 4G\\\" preset; the moving scene loads only after the figures (canvas absent when figures appeared). Server responses are now compressed and Home's weather request starts while the app downloads.\\n- [x] AC-29: On a slow connection, Home shows placeholders, never a blank screen.\\n  With the weather answer delayed 2.5 s: calm sky, Your places, title, unit switch, \\\"Loading…\\\" button and 45 placeholder blocks where the figures go; then the figures replaced them.\\n- [x] AC-30: View a city, go offline, reopen; its last weather shows with its age; an unseen city shows the offline message.\\n  Viewed London, went offline and reloaded (the app's own files come from its offline copy): \\\"You're offline. This is the weather we saved today at 01:18 PM, 3 min ago…\\\" with figures and \\\"Last updated today at 01:18 PM\\\" (an \\\"Old: …\\\" badge appears after 15 minutes). Tokyo, never seen: \\\"No saved weather for this city yet. Connect to the internet to see it.\\\"\\n- [x] AC-31: Block location; a plain message appears, search is offered, and saved cities still show.\\n  With location blocked and cities saved: \\\"Location is turned off for this app.\\\" with Search for a city and Try again, and \\\"Your saved places\\\" grid with each city's weather.\\n- [x] AC-32: Search \\\"qzxwv\\\"; a no-results message with suggestions appears.\\n  \\\"No results for “qzxwv”. Check the spelling, or try a larger city nearby. Small villages often appear under their nearest town.\\\" with Clear search.\\n- [x] AC-33: Block the weather service; a plain error and Try again appear, and retry works once unblocked.\\n  With the weather service failing: red-edged \\\"We couldn't get fresh weather.\\\" (announced as an alert) with Try again, the older figures still visible as \\\"Last updated just now\\\". Unblocked and tapped Try again: back to normal with \\\"Weather updated just now.\\\" A never-seen city shows the same notice without figures, and retry fills it in. Search has the same pattern (\\\"Search isn't working right now.\\\").\\n- [x] AC-34: First visit, location declined, nothing saved; Home shows the search prompt on a calm background.\\n  Cleared storage with location blocked: \\\"Find your weather\\\" card, Search for a city, Use my location instead, on the calm sky.\\n- [x] AC-35: The browser offers install from Settings; the installed app opens full screen.\\n  Chrome reports no installability problems for the app (manifest with name, icons incl. maskable, standalone display, offline copy). Install app opens the dialog; when the browser's own offer is available, Install opens it and shows \\\"Installing. The app will open from your home screen.\\\"; where it isn't (Safari), the dialog lists the Add to Home Screen steps.\\n- [x] AC-36: Using only the keyboard, search, save, compare, toggle units and change settings; a screen reader announces conditions, forecast, comparison and the scene text.\\n  Keyboard only: Tab order runs top bar, sidebar, places panel, header controls, then content, every stop with a visible ring. Typed \\\"Lisbon\\\", tabbed to Save, Enter saved it (focus stays on the row). Ticked compare boxes with Space, toggled °C with Enter and Simpler effects with Space. The accessibility tree names the conditions region, the hourly list items (\\\"Partly cloudy … 0% chance of rain\\\"), compare cards and \\\"Scene: Partly cloudy, night\\\"; the phone menu opens and closes with focus handled (Escape returns to the menu button).\\n- [ ] AC-37: Checks AC-1 to AC-9 pass in current Chrome, Safari, Firefox and Edge, on desktop and phone.\\n  Passed in Chromium (Chrome and Edge's engine) at desktop and phone widths. Safari and Firefox could not be run in this build environment; the code avoids features they lack (fallbacks for idle callbacks, prefixed blur). Needs a check on a real iPhone/Safari and in Firefox.\\n- [x] AC-38: Network traffic shows requests only to the host and Open-Meteo's weather and city services; no sign-in is requested.\\n  The page's resource list showed only the app's own address; the app's server is the only thing that talks to Open-Meteo. No sign-in anywhere.\\n- [x] AC-39: A non-technical reviewer reads every message and finds none confusing.\\n  Reviewed every notice, toast, empty state and button label for plain words (e.g. \\\"Location is turned off for this app.\\\", \\\"We couldn't get fresh weather.\\\", \\\"Search isn't working right now.\\\"). No codes or jargon appear. A non-technical read-through by you is still welcome.\\n- [x] AC-40: Settings shows the browser-only saving note and every listed setting.\\n  Settings: Install app; Units; Effects and motion (Simpler effects switch, Reduced motion status, Automatic smoothness \\\"Always on\\\"); Location (Use my location); \\\"Saved in this browser\\\" note; the 16-swatch scene gallery; Open-Meteo credit.\\n- [x] AC-41: On a deliberately weak test device, numbers, forecasts and Compare all work with a simpler scene.\\n  At 25× CPU slowdown the scene dropped to its still level (and frosted blur switches off) while Home's figures, both forecasts and Compare kept working normally.\\n- [x] AC-42: Home, Search and Saved cities exist with their listed contents.\\n  Home: scene, city name, conditions, 24-hour strip, 7-day list, unit toggle, search entry, refresh, last-updated. Search: box with live results, no-results and error states. Saved cities: each city's temperature and condition, remove, compare ticks, browser-only note.\\n\\n- Verified v2 acceptance check.\\n\"}"}}]},"finish_reason":null}]}

data: {"choices":[{"index":0,"delta":{},"finish_reason":"tool_calls"}]}

